SUMMARY:Storytelling at the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:      This program has a little bit of everythi
 ng for booklovers and storytellers!    Take home a custom typewriter poem
  from the Bloomington Writer's Guild or try your hand at typing one yours
 elf!      Feeling inspired by poetry? Create a tiny keepsake with our pic
 ture frame poetry craft!      Make a book nook to liven up your bookshelv
 es and decorate a bookplate to add to your favorite novel.      Intereste
 d in the ancient art of writing and storytelling? Make your own cuneiform
  tablet out of clay!      Snack on some gourmet cookies and pies while ge
 tting your creativity flowing.            This program is free and open t
 o all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for the entirety of the even
 t to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhibitions.    &#160\;Park
 ing Information:Limitedcomplimentary parkingis available in front of theM
 useum entranceoff Indiana Avenue. Street parking is free on weekdays afte
 r 5:00 PM in the neighborhoods surrounding the Museum. Paid parking optio
 ns include theUniversity Collections at McCallaparking lot off Indiana Av
 enue\, theIndiana Memorial Unionvisitor lot\, and nearby metered street p
 arking.Convenient metered street parking is available in the downtown/Sam
 ple Gates area along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\
 , North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Quest
 ions?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, pleas
 e reach out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or
